  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.34 Continuous emissions monitoring system (CEMS)",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.34 “Continuous emissions monitoring system (CEMS)” means a “continuous emissions monitoring system (CEMS)” as defined in Env-A 101.53. For the purposes of this chapter, this means the equipment required under Env-A 4609 to sample, analyze, measure, and provide, by means of readings recorded at least once every 15 minutes, using an automated DAHS as defined in Env-A 4602.11, a permanent record of, as applicable, stack gas volumetric flow rate, stack gas moisture content, and oxygen or carbon dioxide concentration, in a manner consistent with 40 CFR Part 75 and Env-A 4609.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.33); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.35)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
